(BUF-46: after `Free`, a byte read on the buffer (`byte 1 of X`) is
 refused with the error flag and — per the OOB-read contract elsewhere
 in this section (BUF-26) — returns 0, since a freed buffer's size is 0
 and every position is now out of bounds.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox BUF-46.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   byte-read refused
   0
)
a buffer called line is "hello".
Free line.
a number called b is byte 1 of line.
On error print "byte-read refused".
print b.
